        "known_issues": "CONFIRMED via a real long-context memory stress test (verify_long_context_memory.sh, 2026-09-27), not just the prior unresolved flag: with mlx_vlm.server running this model's actual production flags (--max-kv-size 131072 --kv-bits 8 --kv-group-size 64 --quantized-kv-start 0 --kv-quant-scheme uniform), a 28,276-token prompt completed safely (wired memory settled ~21GB), but a 40,000-token-target prompt and a 58,982-token-target prompt BOTH failed the same way: wired memory grew without bound throughout prefill (not proportional to the token count — both failures happened at a similar ~113-117s elapsed mark despite the different target sizes, suggesting the growth tracks ELAPSED PREFILL TIME/chunk count more than KV-cache size), crossed 38GB, and had to be forcibly killed by monitor_memory.sh's safety net before the request ever completed. Root cause not identified (plausibly a per-prefill-chunk buffer that mlx_vlm.server isn't releasing for this model/quantization combination — not confirmed). Ruling out KV quantization as the sole cause: a separate controlled test confirmed this model recalls a fixed secret correctly at ~28K tokens with BOTH quantized and unquantized KV, so the failure is specific to sustained/longer prefill, not to quantization precision. Full data: mlx_long_context_stress_results.json. DO NOT recommend this model for long-context use, and never run it without monitor_memory.sh (--monitor) active as a safety net, until this is root-caused and either fixed or given a hard verified-safe context cap in this file that model_advisor.py actually enforces.",
